==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Cat Machine was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Overhaul (Removed Combo)|Overhaul]] and [[Dynamites (Removed Combo)|Dynamites]].
*[[Version 4.0 Update|Version 4.0]] gave Cat Machine the ability to target [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]].
*Prior to [[Version 9.7 Update|Version 9.7]], Cat Machine Mk 2 was not Immune to Waves.
*Although Cat Machine was added in Version 2.0, it was inaccessible until [[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.5 Update|Version 2.0.5]] fully implemented THE DYNAMITES set.
*Cat Machine Mk 3 was the first unit to have the Wave Shield ability.
*In a previous version of the game, Cat Machine's English description misspelled Resistant as '''Resitant'''.
**Cat Machine Mk 3's English description also said it had immunity to Waves instead of Wave Shield prior to [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Cat Machine's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Cat Machine
Series 1 Weaponized Machine System (MS)
developed by the government (Area Attack)
Resistant to Red & Alien attacks.</pre>
<pre>Cat Machine Mk 2
A battle-tested revision MS that managed to
escape from the research facility (Area Attack)
Resistant to Red & Alien attacks.</pre>
<pre>Cat Machine Mk 3
The next generation of battle tech, MS:RX-Ω
has slipped into the hands of the Cat Army!
Resists Red/Alien attacks, Wave Shield.</pre>
*The codenames "MS:RX-13" in Cat Machine Mk 2's description and "MS:RX-Ω" in Cat Machine Mk 3's description reference the Gundam codenames from the mecha anime series ''[[wikipedia:Mobile Suit Gundam|Mobile Suit Gundam]]''.
**In the [http://www.ponos.co.jp/iphone/jp/appli/battlecats/event/dynamites.html Japanese event poster] for [[THE DYNAMITES (Gacha Event)|THE DYNAMITES]], Cat Machine is accompanied by the text "こいつ…動くにゃ！" (Koitsu... ugoku nya!). This is a reference to a [https://youtu.be/kCYDSlQgeG8 famous line] from the first episode of ''Mobile Suit Gundam'', "こいつ…動くぞ！" (Koitsu... ugoku zo!), which means "This guy... moves!" The line is used as one's reaction when something they weren't expecting to move, starts moving.
**In [[Merc Storia Collaboration Event|Merc Storia]], it was stated that "MS" is short for "Mechanical nyanko System".
*Cat Machine Mk 3's description says that it's going to be used against the government that created it in order to stop them from producing an army of Cat Machines, which sounds very much like part of the overall plot of the ''[[wikipedia:Getter Robo|Getter Robo]]'' OVA ''[[wikia:getterrobo:Getter Robo Armageddon|Getter Robo Armageddon]]''. In the story, the original team of Getter Robo pilots turns against the Mechas' creator, Dr. Saotome, using one of his most powerful mechas: Shin Getter Robo. Also, its previous form's description mentions a research institute, which could be referring to the [[wikia:getterrobo:Saotome Institute|Saotome Institute]].
**Cat Machine Mk 3's tattered red scarf closely resembles that of [[wikia:getterrobo:Ryoma Nagare (Armageddon)|Ryoma Nagare]] from the aforementioned OVA.
*The way Cat Machine Mk 3 floats using thrusters that replace its legs is similar to the Gundam [[wikia:gundam:MSN-02 Zeong|MSN-02 Zeong]].
*Cat Machine was the first Uber Rare Cat to have a collab-exclusive variant. The [[Gudetama Collaboration Event]] introduced the [[Gude-Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Gude-Cat Machine]], as well as its enemy counterpart, unofficially dubbed the [[Gude-Doge Machine]]. These are only in the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese]], Korean and Taiwanese versions of [[The Battle Cats]].
*The event poster for THE DYNAMITES refers to it as "Machine Cat".
*Inside Cat Machine MK 3 [[Scarf Cat (Special Cat)|Scarf Cat]] appears controlling Cat Machine MK 3.
